    Currently most ATSC 3.0 signals from major networks like NBC have DRM. This is annoying becuase DRM is bad.<br/>
    Many TV sets do not let people watch DRM-Encumbered ATSC 3.0 signals without internet accses.
    The DRM blocks standard TV equipment like DVRs and VCRs preventing people from recording something and watching it later.<br/>
    The FCC should block all DRM on public TV signals.

    Another problem is that TV and Set Top Box makers will likely need to pay for a decryption key to display DRM-encumbered streams.<br/>
    This would increase the prices of TVs.
    
    DRM advocates claim that this is nessisary to stop rebroadcasting of the TV signals. However people can still use a capture card. <br/>
    DRM harms consumers.

    Another bad feature of ATSC 3.0 DRM is that it sometimes adds required intrenet connectivity.